  <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="Tag2195" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;!--?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="no"?--&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style="font-family: Calibri; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;
&lt;div class="Section_1"&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 14pt; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 15pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase;"&gt;DESERET GENERATION&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase;"&gt;&amp;amp; TRANSMISSION COOPERATIVE&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase;"&gt;NOTES TO FINANCIAL STATEMENTS&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 24pt; page-break-after: avoid; border-bottom: 0.75pt solid #000000; padding-bottom: 1pt; font-size: 12pt; -aw-border-bottom: 0.5pt single;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase;"&gt;AS OF AND FOR THE YEARS ENDED DECEMBER&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase;"&gt;31, 2025 and 2024&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt; text-indent: -21.6pt; page-break-after: avoid; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'decimal'; -aw-list-number-values: '1'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 13.09pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase;"&gt;1.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 13.09pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase;"&gt;SUMMARY OF SIGNIFICANT ACCOUNTING POLICIES&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Organization and Purpose&lt;/font&gt;&amp;#8212;Deseret Generation&amp;#160;&amp;amp; Transmission Cooperative (&amp;#8220;Deseret&amp;#8221;) is an electric generation and transmission cooperative organized as a Non&amp;#8209;Profit Corporation under the laws of the State of Utah. Deseret owns 100% of the membership interests in Blue Mountain Energy,&amp;#160;Inc. (BME) (collectively referred to as the &amp;#8220;Cooperative&amp;#8221;). Deseret provides wholesale electric service to five&amp;#160;member distribution cooperatives (collectively, the &amp;#8220;Members&amp;#8221;) engaged in the retail sale of electric energy to member consumers located in Utah, Arizona, Colorado, Nevada, and Wyoming. In addition, Deseret sells wholesale electric service to other nonrelated entities (&amp;#8220;Nonmembers&amp;#8221;). BME provides coal to the Deseret operated Bonanza Plant under a full cost, take&amp;#8209;or&amp;#8209;pay contract with Deseret. The Cooperative&amp;#8217;s accounting policies and records are net of any undivided ownership interests in the Bonanza power plant and transmission lines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Basis of Accounting&lt;/font&gt;&amp;#8212;These regulatory basis financial statements have been prepared for the purpose of complying with, and on the basis of accounting practices specified by the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (&amp;#8220;FERC&amp;#8221;). Accordingly, the FERC Form 1 does not require the accounts of the BME subsidiary to be consolidated in accordance with accounting principles generally accepted in the United States of America (GAAP). Instead, the FERC Form 1 reflects Deseret&amp;#8217;s investment in BME&amp;#8217;s equity and the undistributed retained earnings or accumulated losses of BME in the balance sheet-regulatory basis and Deseret&amp;#8217;s equity in earnings of BME in the statement of income-regulatory basis. In addition, the current portion of long-term debt is classified as long-term debt in the FERC Form 1 and deferred tax assets and liabilities are reported on a gross (versus net) basis, which are not in accordance with GAAP.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Use of Estimates&lt;/font&gt;&amp;#8212;The preparation of financial statements requires the Cooperative to make estimates and assumptions that affect the reported amounts of assets and liabilities and disclosure of contingent assets and liabilities at the date of the financial statements and the reported amounts of revenues and expenses during the reporting period. Actual results could differ from those estimates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Concentration of Revenues&lt;/font&gt;&amp;#8212; During the year ended December&amp;#160;31, 2025, three Member customers generated approximately 29%, 16% and 13% of total operating revenues. During the year ended December&amp;#160;31, 2024, one Nonmember customer generated approximately 13% of total operating revenues, and three Member customers generated approximately 23%, 13% and 10% of total operating revenues.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Concentration of Accounts Receivable&lt;/font&gt;&amp;#8212; As of December&amp;#160;31, 2025, two Member customers represented approximately 36% and 14% of total accounts receivable. As of December&amp;#160;31, 2024, two Member customers represented approximately 33% and 12% of total accounts receivable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Accounts Payable to Related Parties&lt;/font&gt;&amp;#8212;As of December&amp;#160;31, 2025 and 2024, accounts payable included approximately $7,460,000 and $7,460,000, respectively, owed by Deseret to its Members.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Accounting Regulation&lt;/font&gt;&amp;#8212;Deseret is regulated by and maintains its accounts in accordance with the uniform system of accounts prescribed by FERC.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Revenue Recognition&lt;/font&gt;&amp;#8212;The Cooperative recognizes operating revenues from wholesale electricity sales and electricity transmission services in an amount that reflects the consideration to which the Cooperative expects to be entitled in exchange for those sales and services.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt;"&gt;The Cooperative supplies power requirements (energy and demand) to its Members subject to substantially identical wholesale power contracts. The Cooperative also supplies power (energy and demand) to Nonmembers subject to wholesale power contracts. The FERC has granted the Cooperative the right to enter into market&amp;#8209;based rate contracts for its Member and Nonmember customers. Member revenue is recorded at FERC&amp;#8209;authorized rates, and Nonmember revenue is generally recorded at contractual rates. Based on the invoice practical expedient, revenue is recognized equal to the amount the Cooperative has the right to invoice. The Cooperative bills its Members monthly, and payments are due monthly. Substantially all of the Cooperative&amp;#8217;s accounts receivable relate to revenues under its contracts with Members and Nonmembers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Carrying Value of Long&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#8209;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Term Assets&lt;/font&gt;&amp;#8212;The Cooperative evaluates its long&amp;#8209;term assets for impairment whenever events or changes in circumstances indicate that the carrying amount of such assets may not be recoverable. Recoverability of assets to be held and used is measured by a comparison of the carrying amount of the long&amp;#8209;term asset (asset group) to the future undiscounted net cash flows expected to be generated by the asset (asset group). If such assets are considered to be impaired, the impairment to be recognized is measured by the amount by which the carrying amount of the assets exceeds the fair value of the assets. There were no assets impaired during the years ended December&amp;#160;31, 2025 and 2024.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Utility Plant and Mine&lt;/font&gt;&amp;#8212;The utility plant and the Deserado mine are stated at the purchase price. Additions to the utility plant and mine are stated at cost which represents the actual cost of labor, materials, and indirect costs, such as engineering, supervision, transportation, and allowance for borrowed funds used during construction. The Cooperative capitalized interest expense totaling approximately $1,059,000 and $359,000 for the years ended December&amp;#160;31, 2025 and 2024, respectively.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Depreciation, Depletion, and Amortization&lt;/font&gt;&amp;#8212;Depreciation of utility plant is provided using the straight&amp;#8209;line method at rates, which are designed to depreciate the cost of the utility plant over its estimated useful life. The provision for depreciation averaged 2.3% and 2.5% of the depreciable utility plant balance in service for the years ended December&amp;#160;31, 2025 and 2024, respectively.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt;"&gt;General plant assets, such as furniture, equipment, and vehicles are depreciated using the straight&amp;#8209;line method over the estimated useful life of 7 to 10&amp;#160;years.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt;"&gt;The recorded cost of retired utility plant and removal costs less salvage value is charged to accumulated depreciation upon retirement of utility plant in service.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Allowance for Doubtful Accounts&lt;/font&gt;&amp;#8212;The allowance for doubtful accounts is based on a periodic evaluation of the collectability of individual accounts receivable. There has been no significant history of credit losses, as of December&amp;#160;31, 2025 and 2024, there was no allowance for doubtful accounts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Inventory&lt;/font&gt;&amp;#8212;Fuel, spare parts, and supplies inventory are valued at the lower of cost, on a first&amp;#8209;in/first&amp;#8209;out basis, and net realizable value. As of December&amp;#160;31, 2025 and 2024, fuel, spare parts, and supplies inventory are presented net of write-downs of approximately $3,138,000 and $3,151,000, respectively.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Deferred Debits&lt;/font&gt;&amp;#8212;Deferred debits consist primarily of costs that have been deferred and will be amortized in future periods. The Cooperative regularly reviews costs recorded as deferred debits for impairment and during the years ended December&amp;#160;31, 2025 and 2024, there were no impairments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Income Taxes&lt;/font&gt;&amp;#8212;The Cooperative was incorporated under the Non&amp;#8209;profit Corporation and Cooperative Association Act of the State of Utah. The Cooperative received an Internal Revenue Service (IRS) ruling that it is a taxable cooperative. Accordingly, the Cooperative is entitled to exclude the amount of patronage allocations to Members from gross income. Income and expenses related to Nonmember operations are taxable to the Cooperative. The Cooperative files a consolidated tax return.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt;"&gt;The Cooperative uses an asset and liability approach for financial accounting and reporting for income taxes. Deferred income taxes reflect the net tax effects of temporary differences between the carrying amounts of assets and liabilities for financial and tax reporting purposes. A valuation allowance is established when it is more likely than not that some portion or all of the deferred tax assets will not be realized. As of December&amp;#160;31, 2025 and 2024, there is no valuation allowance recorded.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt;"&gt;The Cooperative has analyzed filing positions in the U.S. Federal and state jurisdictions where it is required to file income tax returns, as well as all open tax years in these jurisdictions. The Cooperative believes it has made adequate provisions for income tax positions. The aggregate amount of any additional tax liabilities that may result from examinations, if any, is not expected to have a material adverse effect on the financial results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Statements of Cash Flows&lt;/font&gt;&amp;#8212;The Cooperative considers all highly liquid investments purchased with an original maturity of three&amp;#160;months or less to be cash and cash equivalents.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt; page-break-after: avoid;"&gt;Unrestricted and restricted cash and cash equivalents reported in the balance sheets sum to the same amounts shown in the statements of cash flows as follows:&lt;/p&gt;
