&lt;td class="xl97" style="border-bottom: 2.8pt double #000000; border-top: 1pt solid #000000; height: 12px; width: 106.787px;"&gt;&amp;#160; $ 32,886,912&amp;#160;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;

&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 30.25pt; margin-bottom: 9pt;"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Cash and Investments&lt;/font&gt;&amp;#8212;The Cooperative restricts from the calculation of Available Extra Cash Flow (see Note&amp;#160;4), as allowed by its creditor, cash and investments used for working capital, customer deposits, and other preference items. Cash and investments not restricted for such purposes are classified as unrestricted.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Trading Securities&lt;/font&gt;&amp;#8212;The Cooperative invests in highly&amp;#8209;rated short&amp;#8209;duration securities for cash management, liquidity, and principal preservation. These securities are accounted for as &amp;#8220;trading&amp;#8221;, and as such, changes in the market value are reflected in the statements of revenue and expenses. Unrealized gain of approximately $137,000 and unrealized gain of approximately $416,000 were included in earnings during 2025 and 2024, respectively.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Comprehensive Income&lt;/font&gt;&amp;#8212;The Cooperative had no components of comprehensive income other than net income during 2025 and 2024.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Derivative and Hedging Activities&lt;/font&gt;&amp;#8212;The Cooperative has derivative commodity contracts for the physical delivery of quantities transacted in the normal course of business, which are treated as normal purchases and sales and are not reflected on the balance sheets at fair value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Asset Retirement Obligations&lt;/font&gt;&amp;#8212;The Cooperative records asset retirement obligations where there is a legal obligation associated with the retirement of its tangible long&amp;#8209;lived assets and where the amounts are estimable. The carrying amount of the liability for asset retirement obligations (&amp;#8220;ARO&amp;#8221;) is adjusted upon revisions to the timing or the amount of the future cash flows estimated to settle such obligations. Associated increases or decreases in such obligations are correspondingly recorded as increases or decreases to the related assets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Recently Issued Accounting Standards&lt;/font&gt;&amp;#8212;In December 2023, the FASB issued ASU&amp;#160;2023-09, Income Taxes (Topic&amp;#160;740). ASU&amp;#160;2023-09 is effective for annual reporting periods beginning after December&amp;#160;15, 2025. The standard requires disaggregated information about a reporting entity&amp;#8217;s effective tax rate reconciliation as well as information on income taxes paid. The Cooperative does not expect the adoption to have a material impact on its financial statements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt; text-indent: -21.6pt; page-break-after: avoid; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'decimal'; -aw-list-number-values: '2'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 13.09pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase;"&gt;2.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 13.09pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase;"&gt;UTILITY PLANT&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt;"&gt;Construction of the Bonanza Plant, a coal&amp;#8209;fired electric generating unit located near Vernal, Utah, was completed in late 1985 and the plant was placed in commercial operation in 1986. In December 1985, the Cooperative sold a 1.875%, 3.75%, and 6.25% undivided interest in the Bonanza Plant consisting of common facilities, generating plant, and transmission facility, respectively, to Utah Municipal Power Agency (UMPA) for approximately $28,506,000, which represented the Cooperative&amp;#8217;s actual cost. Pursuant to a Management Agreement, UMPA reimburses the Cooperative for the operating expenses related to its undivided interest.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt;"&gt;The Cooperative owns a 25.1% undivided interest in an electric generating unit (&amp;#8220;Hunter&amp;#160;II&amp;#8221;) located in Emery County, Utah, which is operated by PacifiCorp under an Ownership and Management Agreement dated October&amp;#160;24, 1980. The agreement for operation of the generating unit provides that the Cooperative pay certain operating expenses related to the undivided interest owned by the Cooperative.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt; text-indent: -21.6pt; page-break-after: avoid; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'decimal'; -aw-list-number-values: '3'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 13.09pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase;"&gt;3.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 13.09pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase;"&gt;PATRONAGE CAPITAL&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt;"&gt;In accordance with the Cooperative&amp;#8217;s by&amp;#8209;laws, taxable Member margins are allocated or allocable to the Members based upon the patronage of the Members. Taxable Member margins are used to reduce any previously incurred accumulated member deficit until eliminated. Taxable Nonmember margins are first used to offset previously incurred accumulated Nonmember deficit, and to the extent not needed for this purpose, may be used to offset any Member accumulated losses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt; page-break-after: avoid;"&gt;Patronage capital as of December&amp;#160;31, 2025 and 2024, comprised the following:&lt;/p&gt;
